Ours (dsv41 recipe), Apache-2.0, against vLLM main 6e517b15 + patches 0001-0021 + 0023-0036 (touches
v1/attention/backends/mla/sparse_swa.py and v1/worker/gpu/attn_utils.py). VLLM_DSV41_SWA_BATCH=1 (default 0): in a
pure-decode step, DeepSeek-V4.1's SWA metadata build of every KV cache group (a torch.ge for is_valid_token, a fill of
the decode lens' tail and _compute_swa_indices_and_lens_kernel, per group) is queued by DeepseekSparseSWAMetadataBuilder
.build inside build_attn_metadata's loop (sparse_swa.deferred_decode_builds) and run after it as one
_swa_decode_batched_kernel launch per batch of groups that share shapes and the batch-level tensors (a table of each
group's buffer addresses, uploaded once per layout and cached: the buffers are persistent). Same arithmetic, same
buffers, bit for bit; prefill and mixed batches, non-causal (DSpark) builds and graph captures keep the per-group path.
VLLM_DSV41_SWA_BATCH_FILE=<path> (measurement knob): "1" / "0" in the file switches the batching while serving, read
every 16 builds when its mtime moved (each rank its own copy: both paths write the same bits), for an A/B in one boot.
Why: the next round's input prep is 109 eager launches on GB10, ~4 us apart, 57 of them these builds (19 groups x 3):
~0.2 ms a round on every prompt (Oct 21 prose trace).
Test: patches/tests/test_dsv41_swa_batch.py (serve image).

